### 1. Iterative Approach (The most fundamental way)

This method manually iterates through the string until it finds the null terminator (`\0`).

```c
#include <stddef.h> // For size_t (good practice for lengths)

/**
 * @brief Calculates the length of a null-terminated string without using strlen.
 * 
 * @param str The string to measure.
 * @return size_t The length of the string (number of characters before the null terminator).
 */
size_t my_strlen(const char *str) {
    if (str == NULL) {
        return 0; // Handle null pointer input gracefully
    }

    size_t length = 0;
    // Loop until the current character is the null terminator ('\0')
    while (str[length] != '\0') {
        length++;
    }
    return length;
}

